00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:58.304
If I don't think he should be president.

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.373
And it's going to be a very tough thing

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:02.408
for some of these candidates

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:02.842
who are going

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:04.911
to have to decide from their perspective

00:09:05.111 --> 00:09:07.213
if they are going to put country first

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:08.281
or party first.

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:10.716
And that is kind of the calculus

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:11.751
that is going on.

00:09:11.751 --> 00:09:12.318
Not among

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:14.186
all of the Republican candidates

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:15.421
who are not Donald Trump

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:16.355
but among some of them.

00:09:16.355 --> 00:09:17.356
Never mind

00:09:17.356 --> 00:09:18.991
the question that I put in the clip

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:19.892
that you played

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.294
about Trump himself,

00:09:21.294 --> 00:09:22.828
whether he will actually stick

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:23.763
to any kind of pledge.

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.831
They signed pledges in 2016.

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.633
It's not really clear

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:29.001
that they actually lived up to it.

00:09:29.001 --> 00:09:30.136
John Kasich

00:09:30.136 --> 00:09:30.937
signed that pledge

00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:31.904
to get on the debate stage

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:33.272
and he never supported Donald Trump.

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:34.240
Just one example.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.107
Yeah, it's a great point

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:36.409
that it's not just about Trump

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:37.176
and what he does.

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:39.345
It's also what Asa Hutchinson and others.

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:41.547
One fascinating part of this interview,

00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:42.748
I thought was where she brought up

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:44.283
the fact that she's Mitt Romney's niece.

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:46.919
Something that we sat down play at times

00:09:47.186 --> 00:09:48.554
and she said, I'm Mitt Romney's niece.

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.256
I was appointed to the RNC by Trump.

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:51.724
She was
I would support both of them

00:09:51.724 --> 00:09:52.558
if they were the nominee,

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:53.492
but I don't know

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:54.660
if they would support each other.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:55.861
Talking about how damaging

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:57.463
all of this is for Republicans

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:58.864
generally, that they're not

00:09:58.864 --> 00:10:00.232
that they don't know for sure that they

00:10:00.232 --> 00:10:01.500
support who the nominee is.

00:10:02.468 --> 00:10:03.302
Yeah, I really

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:04.437
thought that was interesting.

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:07.807
As well, because she was trying

00:10:07.807 --> 00:10:11.210
to make the point that she is a unifier

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.044
and she is

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:14.914
somebody who can kind of see broadly

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:17.650
on the entire Republican spectrum.

00:10:18.184 --> 00:10:20.820
But look, again, it is damaging

00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:22.822
because we're talking about

00:10:22.822 --> 00:10:24.390
the influence of one man,

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.524
and that is Donald Trump.

00:10:25.524 --> 00:10:26.258
If Donald Trump

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:27.727
were not part of this equation

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:29.328
and you're talking about

00:10:29.328 --> 00:10:30.329
Ron DeSantis,

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:32.431
Asa Hutchinson, Chris Sununu,

00:10:32.431 --> 00:10:33.499
you know, Chris Christie,

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:35.234
name your candidate.

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:36.702
They would all be fine

00:10:36.702 --> 00:10:38.971
with signing a loyalty pledge.

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:40.740
This is about Donald Trump

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.076
and about the events of January six.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:44.944
Full stop.

